**Status:** 🧹 PLANNING - Cleanup needed, distributed backup desired

**Goal:** Clean NAS (remove unused apps), implement encrypted distributed backup across friend nodes

**Part 1: Cleanup**
- Audit running containers (via Portainer)
- Remove unused apps (LibreChat confirmed for deletion)
- Apply NAS best practices (storage organization, retention policies)
- Free up space for backups

**Part 2: Distributed Backup System**
- **Your nodes:** NAS (Brooklyn) + friend's NAS (Germany) + friend's NAS (Brazil)
- **Goal:** Encrypted offsite backups across friend nodes
- **Technology:** Likely **ZFS snapshots** + **rclone/restic/borg** for encrypted sync

**Backup tools to evaluate:**
- **ZFS:** Snapshots + send/receive (native encryption)
- **Restic:** Encrypted, deduplicated, multi-backend
- **Borg:** Fast, encrypted, deduplicated backups
- **rclone:** Sync to remote storage (encrypt on-the-fly)
- **Syncthing:** Already installed, P2P encrypted sync

**Distributed backup model:**
- Each NAS backs up to 2 other nodes (redundancy)
- Encrypted at rest (friends can't read your data)
- Automated sync (daily/weekly snapshots)
- Space sharing agreement (e.g., 500GB each)

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Audit NAS: list all running apps/containers
- [ ] Delete unused apps (LibreChat + others)
